{%- comment -%}
  Emits inline custom properties for a section's vertical padding.

  The merchant picks a named step, not a pixel figure — see space-step.liquid
  for the steps and for why they carry the design's whole clamp() triple
  rather than a single number.

  This snippet used to take a desktop figure and derive the rest: a floor at a
  flat 60% of it, and a slope from (figure - floor) / the 360-1440 span. That
  is three of the design's decisions replaced by one of the merchant's, and it
  did not reproduce the design at any width. Measured against the design's own
  home page, five of seven sections were 20-24px short at the ceiling while
  carrying more padding than the design in the middle of the range, because a
  derived slope ramps from the first pixel where the design holds a floor and
  then climbs steeply. Most Loved and The Craft happened to land close and
  the rest did not, which is the shape of a value nobody checked.

  Accepts:
    padding_top    - a step name. Falls back to the global default.
    padding_bottom - a step name. Falls back to the global default.

  Usage:
    <section style="{% render 'section-style', padding_top: section.settings.padding_top %}">
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign pt_step = padding_top | default: settings.section_padding_default
  assign pb_step = padding_bottom | default: settings.section_padding_default
-%}
{%- capture pt -%}{%- render 'space-step', step: pt_step -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture pb -%}{%- render 'space-step', step: pb_step -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- comment -%}
  An unrecognised step prints nothing, so fall back to the design's commonest
  section rhythm rather than emitting an empty length — `--pad-top: ;` is an
  invalid declaration and would take the padding with it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if pt == blank -%}{%- capture pt -%}{%- render 'space-step', step: 'lg' -%}{%- endcapture -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if pb == blank -%}{%- capture pb -%}{%- render 'space-step', step: 'lg' -%}{%- endcapture -%}{%- endif -%}
--pad-top: {{ pt }}; --pad-bottom: {{ pb }};
